# Databricks notebook source
# MAGIC %md
# MAGIC # AID Code Dictionary — Load
# MAGIC
# MAGIC | | |
# MAGIC |---|---|
# MAGIC | **Phenotype** | Autoimmune Disease (AID) |
# MAGIC | **Source algorithm** | eMERGE Autoimmune Disease Algorithm V4.0 (July 2017) |
# MAGIC | **Source location** | https://phekb.org/phenotype/755 |
# MAGIC | **Source authors** | Tong, Kiryluk, Petukhova, Wang, Lebwohl, Gharavi, Weng, Hripcsak (Columbia University) |
# MAGIC | **Developer(s)** | Srushti Gangireddy, Wu-Chen Su |
# MAGIC | **Date Created** | 2026-07-28 |
# MAGIC | **Last Modified** | 2026-08-22 |
# MAGIC | **Platform** | Databricks SQL / OMOP CDM |
# MAGIC
# MAGIC ## Purpose
# MAGIC
# MAGIC Builds the value-set reference table `aid_code_dict` that drives
# MAGIC `02_aid_phenotype`. This notebook contains **data only** — no phenotype
# MAGIC logic.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC ## Provenance
# MAGIC
# MAGIC All 47,556 rows come from the coding file shipped with the published
# MAGIC algorithm (`AIDalgorithm_coding_V3b.txt`, §VI item 3 of the source
# MAGIC document), which ships with case rows duplicated 2-4x. The same value
# MAGIC sets are published on OHDSI ATLAS as cohort 102998 (cases) and 919472
# MAGIC (controls). Rows here are **deduplicated**, and the source columns
# MAGIC (`ConceptSetId` / `codeCategory` / `Name` / `conceptId` / `conceptCode` /
# MAGIC `conceptName` / `vocabulary`) are reshaped into the 10 columns below.
# MAGIC `conceptName` is dropped — join to the site `concept` table if names are
# MAGIC needed. No codes were added, removed, or edited.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC ## Schema
# MAGIC
# MAGIC | Column | Meaning |
# MAGIC |---|---|
# MAGIC | `code_role` | Which arm of the algorithm the code serves (see below) |
# MAGIC | `code_category` | Source `codeCategory`, verbatim |
# MAGIC | `variable_name` | Source `Name`, verbatim (e.g. `Endocrine: T1D`) |
# MAGIC | `subphenotype_num` | 1-51, disease index; `NULL` outside `CASE_DISEASE` |
# MAGIC | `group_name` | One of 9 organ-system groups; `NULL` outside `CASE_DISEASE` |
# MAGIC | `disease_name` | Short disease label; `NULL` outside `CASE_DISEASE` |
# MAGIC | `test_key` | Serology assay key (21 values); `NULL` outside `SEROLOGY` |
# MAGIC | `concept_id` | OMOP standard or source concept ID |
# MAGIC | `code` | Native vocabulary code |
# MAGIC | `code_type` | ICD10CM, SNOMED, ICD9CM, Read, OXMIS, LOINC, HCPCS |
# MAGIC
# MAGIC ## Roles
# MAGIC
# MAGIC | `code_role` | Rows | Used by `02_aid_phenotype` |
# MAGIC |---|---|---|
# MAGIC | `CASE_DISEASE` | 1,326 | Yes — case definition, 51 diseases |
# MAGIC | `T2DM` | 182 | Yes — T1D exclusion rule (subphenotype 15 only) |
# MAGIC | `CONTROL_DX` | 45,871 | Yes — control exclusion |
# MAGIC | `SEROLOGY` | 164 | Yes — control exclusion, 21 test keys |
# MAGIC | `IMMUNOGLOBULIN` | 10 | **No** — data-dictionary covariate only |
# MAGIC | `COMPLEMENT` | 3 | **No** — data-dictionary covariate only |
# MAGIC
# MAGIC `IMMUNOGLOBULIN` and `COMPLEMENT` are loaded deliberately. They are
# MAGIC covariates requested by the algorithm's data dictionary (IgA/IgG/IgM and
# MAGIC C3/C4 in mg/dL), not inputs to the case/control decision, so the
# MAGIC phenotype notebook does not read them.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC ## Known dictionary limitations
# MAGIC
# MAGIC Carried from the published coding file; none are corrected here.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC - **6,373 `CONTROL_DX` rows are Read or OXMIS** (UK primary-care
# MAGIC   vocabularies). They resolve in the OMOP vocabulary but match no US
# MAGIC   EHR data.
# MAGIC - **The `CONTROL_DX` set is contaminated.** Of its ICD10CM codes,
# MAGIC   ~19,255 are chapter S (injury/fracture); the ICD9 portion is
# MAGIC   similarly dominated by the 8xx fracture chapters. Applied as
# MAGIC   published, a fracture history alone disqualifies a person from
# MAGIC   control status. Left as published — see notebook 02.
# MAGIC - **All 20 `T2DM` ICD-9 codes are the 250.x0/250.x2 family**, labelled
# MAGIC   "type II *or unspecified type*". ICD-9 gives type II and
# MAGIC   unspecified-type the same fifth digit, so any T1D patient with a
# MAGIC   generic pre-2015 diabetes code trips the T1D exclusion. Left as
# MAGIC   published — see notebook 02.
# MAGIC - **`Cardiolipin_IgA` is in the dictionary but not in Table 3** of the
# MAGIC   algorithm document (which lists IgG and IgM only). Left in.
# MAGIC - **Seven serology variables named in the document's Figure 2
# MAGIC   footnote 4 are absent** from the coding file: islet cell
# MAGIC   (ICA/IA-2/ICA512), GAD, tissue transglutaminase IgA, endomysium
# MAGIC   IgG+IgA, gliadin IgA+IgG, ASCA IgG+IgA, and OmpC+CBir1.
# MAGIC - **Row counts differ from the document**, which states 1,528 case and
# MAGIC   49,960 control codes against 1,326 / 45,871 distinct here. The
# MAGIC   difference is the shipped duplication plus codes that map to the same
# MAGIC   concept.

# COMMAND ----------

# MAGIC %md
# MAGIC ## 1. Target schema

# COMMAND ----------

# MAGIC %sql
# MAGIC CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS workspace_sdphenotypecore.aid;
# MAGIC USE workspace_sdphenotypecore.aid;

# COMMAND ----------

# MAGIC %md
# MAGIC ## 2. Table definition
# MAGIC
# MAGIC Dropped and recreated on every run so the table always reflects exactly
# MAGIC the `INSERT` batches in this notebook.

# COMMAND ----------

# MAGIC %sql
# MAGIC DROP TABLE IF EXISTS workspace_sdphenotypecore.aid.aid_code_dict;
# MAGIC
# MAGIC CREATE TABLE workspace_sdphenotypecore.aid.aid_code_dict (
# MAGIC   code_role        STRING,   -- CASE_DISEASE | T2DM | CONTROL_DX | SEROLOGY | IMMUNOGLOBULIN | COMPLEMENT
# MAGIC   code_category    STRING,   -- source codeCategory, verbatim
# MAGIC   variable_name    STRING,   -- source Name, verbatim
# MAGIC   subphenotype_num INT,      -- 1-51; NULL outside CASE_DISEASE
# MAGIC   group_name       STRING,   -- organ-system group; NULL outside CASE_DISEASE
# MAGIC   disease_name     STRING,   -- short disease label; NULL outside CASE_DISEASE
# MAGIC   test_key         STRING,   -- serology assay key; NULL outside SEROLOGY
# MAGIC   concept_id       BIGINT,   -- OMOP concept ID
# MAGIC   code             STRING,   -- native vocabulary code
# MAGIC   code_type        STRING    -- source vocabulary
# MAGIC );

# COMMAND ----------

# MAGIC %md
# MAGIC ## 3. `CASE_DISEASE` — 1,326 rows
# MAGIC
# MAGIC Diagnosis codes for the 51 constituent autoimmune diseases, grouped
# MAGIC into 9 organ-system groups. `subphenotype_num` is the disease index;
# MAGIC each number maps to exactly one `variable_name`, so counting distinct
# MAGIC qualifying rows per person yields the number of distinct autoimmune
# MAGIC diseases.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC Subphenotype 15 (`Endocrine: T1D`) is the only one subject to the T2DM
# MAGIC exclusion rule applied in notebook 02.

# COMMAND ----------

# MAGIC %sql
# MAGIC -- CASE_DISEASE: 1,326 rows in 3 batches of 500.
