# COMMAND ----------

# MAGIC %md
# MAGIC ## 9. Serology threshold table (fallback, intentionally empty)
# MAGIC
# MAGIC Control Cohort Condition B of the algorithm document delegates serology
# MAGIC positivity to "institutional and assay recommendations" — it supplies no
# MAGIC numeric cutoffs. Notebook 02 therefore reads each measurement's own
# MAGIC `range_high` as the institutional upper limit of normal, and falls back
# MAGIC to this table only where `range_high` is `NULL`.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC The table is created empty. **While it is empty, the fallback arm never
# MAGIC fires**, so numeric results lacking `range_high` are invisible to the
# MAGIC serology gate. On VUMC SD that is ~72,000 rows concentrated in five
# MAGIC assays (dsDNA, SS-A, SS-B, Scl70, Sm); the remaining assays carry
# MAGIC `range_high` on 95-100% of numeric results.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC Populate per `test_key` **and** `unit_source` — these assays run on
# MAGIC incompatible scales, so a single global cutoff is not meaningful.
# MAGIC Cutoffs can be derived from the rows that do carry `range_high` rather
# MAGIC than invented. Autoantibody reference ranges are one-sided, so
# MAGIC `range_low` is deliberately absent.

# COMMAND ----------

# MAGIC %sql
# MAGIC CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS workspace_sdphenotypecore.aid.aid_serology_thresholds (
# MAGIC   test_key      STRING,   -- joins to aid_code_dict.test_key
# MAGIC   unit_source   STRING,   -- matches measurement.unit_source_value; NULL = applies to any unit
# MAGIC   pos_min_value DOUBLE    -- value_as_number >= this is positive
# MAGIC );

# COMMAND ----------

# MAGIC %md
# MAGIC ## 10. Verification
# MAGIC
# MAGIC Expected: 47,556 rows total.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC | `code_role` | `n` |
# MAGIC |---|---|
# MAGIC | `CONTROL_DX` | 45,871 |
# MAGIC | `CASE_DISEASE` | 1,326 |
# MAGIC | `T2DM` | 182 |
# MAGIC | `SEROLOGY` | 164 |
# MAGIC | `IMMUNOGLOBULIN` | 10 |
# MAGIC | `COMPLEMENT` | 3 |

# COMMAND ----------

# MAGIC %sql
# MAGIC SELECT code_role, count(*) AS n
# MAGIC FROM workspace_sdphenotypecore.aid.aid_code_dict
# MAGIC GROUP BY code_role
# MAGIC ORDER BY n DESC;